Now notice that  $(k+1)a_{k+1} - S_{k+1} = ka_{k+1}-S_k + a_{k+1}-a_{k+1}$ . Thus, in fact  $LHS$  of an inequality in this chain is equal to the  $RHS$ , of the inequality below it. Then, by the chain we get that in fact  $a_0 < a_0$ , which is clearly a contradiction. Thus, there is only a unique  $n$  which satisfies the given claim.

