There are a *lot* of proofs of this. Here's one I typed out a few days ago:

Let  $E$  and  $F$  be the foot of the  $B$ -altitude and  $C$ -altitude of  $\triangle ABC$ , and  $M$  be midpoint of  $\triangle ABC$ . The  $ME$  and  $MF$  are tangent to  $\odot(AEF)$ .

*Proof 1.* Let  $\omega$  be the circle through  $B, C, E, F$ .
Note that  $\omega$  is the circle with diameter  $\overline{AB}$ , thus  $M$  is the center of  $\omega$ .
\[\angle EFM = \angle FEM = \frac12(\angle FEM + \angle EMF) = 90^{\circ} - \frac12\angle EMF = 90^{\circ} - \angle EBF = 90^{\circ} - (90^{\circ} - \angle BAC) = \angle BAC\]
[asy]
import geometry;
unitsize(2.5cm);

pair A = dir(108), B = dir(210), C = -1/B;
triangle t = triangle((point) A,(point) B,(point) C);
pair D = foot(t.VA), E = foot(t.VB), F = foot(t.VC);
pair M = (B+C)/2;
perpendicularmark(altitude(t.VB), opposite(t.VB), quarter=-1, 5);
markangle(2, F, E, M, radius = 0.35cm);
markangle(2, E, F, M, radius = -0.35cm);
markangle(2, B, A, C, radius = 0.35cm);

draw(t); draw(circle(M, abs(M-B)), linewidth(0.4)+dashed);
draw(E--M--F--cycle); draw(B--E, dotted);
dot(A^^B^^C); dot(M^^E^^F);
[/asy]

*Proof 2.* Let  $H$  be the orthocenter,  $D$  be the foot of the  $A$ -altitude and  $P$  be the midpoint of  $\overline{AH}$ .
Note that  $P$  is the centre of  $\odot(AEF)$ . Also, note that  $\odot(PEFM)$  is the nine-point circle of triangle  $ABC$ . Thus,
\[90^{\circ} = \measuredangle PDM = \measuredangle PEM.\qquad\blacksquare\]

[asy]
import geometry;

unitsize(2.5cm);
pair A = dir(108), B = dir(210), C = -1/B;
triangle t = triangle((point) A, (point) B, (point) C);
pair H = orthocentercenter(t);
pair M = midpoint(t.BC);
pair D = foot(t.VA), E = foot(t.VB), F = foot(t.VC);
pair P = (A+H)/2;

draw(t); draw(circumcircle((point) A, (point) E, (point) F)); draw(circumcircle((point) M, (point) E, (point) F), linetype("0 2"));
draw(M--E^^M--F); draw(P--D^^P--E^^P--F, dotted);
perpendicularmark(line(P,D), line(M,D), size = 5, quarter=2);
perpendicularmark(line(P,E), line(M,E), size = 5, quarter=3);
perpendicularmark(line(P,F), line(M,F), size = 5, quarter=2);
dot(A^^B^^C); dot(M^^D^^E^^F^^P^^H);
[/asy]

