We claim that the value of  $f_{3, AB} - f_{4, AB} + f_{5, AB} - \cdots $  only depends on the number of points that lie to the right of  $AB$ . We prove this by moving a point  $C$  through  $AB$  and noticing that the desired value stays constant. Let  $\mathcal{D}$  be a convex  $k$ -gon containing  $AB$  as an edge. When we move  $C$  through segment  $AB$ , the number of  $k$ -gons decreases by 1 ( $\mathcal{D}$  itself), but the number of  $(k+1)$ -gons also decreases by 1 ( $\mathcal{D}$  adjoined to  $C$ ); thus,  $f_{3, AB} - f_{4, AB} + f_{5, AB} - \cdots $  stays constant. In addition, if  $C$  moves around on the left without crossing  $AB$ , a similar argument shows that the value stays the same. Hence we may assume that  $A$ ,  $B$ , and all  $p$  points lying to the right of line  $AB$  form a convex  $(p+2)$ -gon, implying that\[f_{3, AB} - f_{4, AB} + f_{5, AB} - f_{6, AB} + \cdots = \binom{p}{1} - \binom{p}{2} + \binom{p}{3} - \cdots\]which is 0 only when  $p = 0$  and 1 when  $p > 0$ . Thus,\[3f_3 - 4f_4 + 5f_5 - 6f_6 + \cdots = 2\binom{n}{2} - C_S,\]where  $n$  is the number of points in  $S$  and  $C_S$  is the number of points on the convex hull of  $S$ . In this problem,  $n = 2014$  and  $\min C_S = 3$ , so our answer is  $2\binom{2014}{2} - 3 = 4054179$ .</details>

