A solution. Not sure if correct or not. So, here goes. After a trivial induction we can show that  $a_n=10^{2^{n}-n-1}\cdot a_1^{2^{n-1}}$ . Now  $\lim_{n\to \infty} a_n=0$ . Then given  $\varepsilon>0$  for large  $n$ , we have 
\begin{align*}
& \frac{(100a_1)^{2^{n-1}}}{10^{n+1}}<\varepsilon
\implies & \log_{10}(100a_1)<\frac{\log_{10}\varepsilon+n+1}{2^{n-1}}
\implies & \lim_{n\to \infty}\log_{10}(100a_1)\le \lim_{n\to \infty} \frac{\log_{10}\varepsilon+n+1}{2^{n-1}}=0
\implies & \log_{10}(100a_1)\le 0\implies a_1\le \frac{1}{100} \end{align*}
