<details><summary>Solution 1</summary>$Q$  is the Miquel point of  $\triangle PAB$  w.r.t  $\triangle XDC$ , so  $ABQX$  is cyclic. Hence  $\angle QXC = \angle PBQ = \angle CDQ$ , which implies  $XDQC$  is cyclic. So  $\angle DQX = \angle DCX = \angle PCA = \angle DPZ$ , and it follows  $\angle DQX + \angle DQZ = 180^{\circ}$ . Hence  $X, Q, Z$  are collinear. Similarly,  $Y, X, Q$  are collinear, which gives the desired result.</details>
<details><summary>Solution 2</summary>$Q$  is the Miquel point of  $\triangle PAB$  w.r.t  $\triangle XDC$ , so  $ABQX$  is cyclic. By Reim's theorem on  $\omega_1$  and  $(ABQX)$ ,  $Q,X,Y$  are collinear; by Reim's theorem on  $\omega_2$  and  $(ABQX)$ ,  $Z,Q,X$  are collinear, and the result follows.</details>
